             has to be planted at the REPOSITORY ROOT, above an unrelated TypeScript/Node application." The
             premise is right — SECTIONS match at or below their own directory — and the conclusion does not
             follow, because analyzer-config DISCOVERY walks the SOURCE FILE's ancestor chain, not the
             project's. A section may therefore sit anywhere at or above the vendored file's real path,
             INCLUDING the directory holding it. Corrected in place rather than replaced, because the false
             version was load-bearing in an owner's artefact and a reader who bookmarked it must see it
             retired. What survives of the objection is a DIFFERENT one, and it is NOT measured: that
