       🔴 AE-1 (.superpowers/sdd/item12-stage2/task-1-brief.md) — owner item 12, STAGE 2. THE SWITCH IS
       STILL OFF. NOT ONE WARNING WAS PAID AND NOT ONE WAS SILENCED. What this round installs is the
       BOOK-KEEPING the decision needs before it can be enforced, and the argument is one measured fact:

           the (a)-vs-(b) choice above puts a population NOBODY MAY PAY — the vendored file's 103 — beside
           a population that stages 4..N exist to PAY DOWN. A single warning TOTAL cannot tell those two
           apart, so a payment of k in ours and a re-vendoring of +k in theirs leave the total unmoved and
           the gate green. That is not a risk of the plan; it is the plan's own shape.

       So scripts/verify-suites.sh now asserts, beside EXPECT_WARNINGS and without touching it, an
       ORIGIN-SPLIT LEDGER: an enumerated map from (bucket, warning code) to count, equality in both
       directions, with VENDORED derived from THIS csproj's own `Compile Include` rather than re-spelled.
       Live today at 82 vendored / 34 ours — the split is not waiting for stage 3, because 82 of the
       current 116 already sit in that file. Run unchanged over the diagnostic command above it splits the
